research/audit/wave6-alpha.md-21-8. `ex-closed-interval-is-perfect` — **concur; `ai-altered`, `established-knowledge`.** Every nondegenerate closed real interval is closed and each of its points, endpoints included, is approached by another point of the interval, so it is the canonical nonempty perfect-set example and is uncountable.
research/audit/wave6-alpha.md-22-9. `cex-closed-bounded-in-q-not-compact` — **concur; `ai-altered`, `established-knowledge`.** The rational lower cut at the missing point `sqrt(2)` is bounded and relatively closed in `Q` but admits the standard increasing open cover with no finite subcover, canonically exhibiting the failure of Heine–Borel without completeness.
research/audit/wave6-alpha.md-23-10. `cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected` — **concur; `ai-altered`, `established-knowledge`.** Splitting `Q ∩ [0,2]` at the absent irrational `sqrt(2)` gives two nonempty separated pieces, the textbook demonstration that rational order-convexity does not imply connectedness in the real subspace topology.
research/audit/wave6-alpha.md-24-11. `cex-unbounded-closed-set-not-compact` — **concur; `ai-altered`, `established-knowledge`.** `Z` is the standard closed unbounded noncompact subset of `R`, and `(0,1)` the standard bounded nonclosed noncompact subset, separately showing that neither Heine–Borel hypothesis may be dropped.
